{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged on identity: trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry trip_id TRP-09115, and the trip_record's started_at (2026-09-22T20:00:00+08:00) matches the gps_trace's first_fix_at (2026-09-22T20:00:00+08:00), so the recorded timestamps agree to the second rather than anywhere near the 10-minute tolerance. These artifacts describe one and the same trip, and nothing on the record suggests otherwise.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09115", "EV-GPS-09115", "EV-FARE-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.optimal_distance_km"
    },
    {
      "text": "A route deviation is established on this trip's own numbers under POL-RD-01: the trace records 15.0 km against a booked optimal of 11.0 km, an excess of 4.0 km, which is 36.36% of optimal. Both POL-RD-01 gates are cleared, because 4.0 km exceeds the 0.8 km absolute threshold and 36.36% exceeds the 20% proportional threshold.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115", "EV-TRIP-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km"
    },
    {
      "text": "The threshold test is run, as POL-RD-01 requires, on gps_trace.trace_distance_km and not on the rounded trip_record convenience copy: the governing trace figure is 15.0 km, and the trip_record's actual_distance_km agrees at 15.0 km, so no rounding disagreement arises on this record and the excess stands at 4.0 km however the two fields are read.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115", "EV-TRIP-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km"
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider discloses, as POL-GEN-02 requires, that the gps_trace is impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: limbs (a) and (b) fire, because there is a single 160-second gap between consecutive fixes (20:03:10 to 20:05:50, above the 90-second limit) and a 1.35 km straight-line step across that gap (above the 500 m limit); limb (c) does not fire, the sampling interval being 10 seconds throughout. The impairment is narrow and bounded rather than systemic: the trace is otherwise continuous with 166 fixes across the trip's 30 minutes, coverage is 91.1%, and the gap's entire straight-line span of 1.35 km is far smaller than the 4.0 km of excess recorded across the trace. The rider asks the judge to weigh the trace with that disclosure in view, not to discard the whole record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "gaps"
    },
    {
      "text": "The chat log is an artifact independent of the trace, and it corroborates a route discontinuity in the same window as the gap: the rider reports at 20:08:20 that the route display jumped away from the booked road, and the driver replies at 20:08:50 that his navigation display also refreshed and that he continued toward the destination. The driver nowhere denies that the vehicle left the booked corridor — his counterparty_statement says only that he cannot independently account for the telemetry gap. If the judge treats the driver's own message as an admission for the purposes of POL-RD-07(ii), the independent-corroboration requirement is satisfied and the deviation stands on the trace together with the chat log.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09115", "EV-GPS-09115", "EV-TRIP-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic-advisory exoneration is available to the driver under POL-RD-03. That clause requires a traffic_advisory naming a road, expressway segment or junction the optimal route traverses, and the only advisory artifact on file, EV-ADVIS-09115-01, carries no payload at all. Absence is citable: no advisory covers this road, so nothing in the record exonerates any part of the 4.0 km excess and the booked optimal of 11.0 km stands as the baseline.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09115-01", "EV-TRIP-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"]
    },
    {
      "text": "No rider-requested-detour exoneration is available under POL-RD-04 either. The clause needs a rider instruction that identifies a place or road specifically enough to act on, corroborated by chat_message.waypoint_hint or by travel over a named road. The chat log contains no such instruction: both messages carry waypoint_hint null and neither names a road. On this record the corroboration test cannot be run, the clause is unavailable, and the case must be decided on the remaining clauses.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Neither relocation nor pooling reduces the baseline. pickup_amended_at and dropoff_amended_at are both null, so POL-RD-05's amended-endpoint re-quote does not exist on this record and the booked optimal of 11.0 km is untouched; and vehicle_type is RYDE_X rather than RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12's matched-itinerary baseline does not apply and solo_optimal_distance_km is irrelevant to the measurement. The excess therefore stands at 4.0 km against the booked 11.0 km optimal.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-05", "POL-RD-12"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The extra corroboration burden POL-RD-08 places on repeat claimants does not touch this rider. It fires only where rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 4 or more and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 1 or fewer; both fields are 0 on this profile, so no additional corroboration beyond the trace is required of this claim. Every other field on the rider profile — prior disputes, lifetime counters, rating — is context only under POL-GEN-01 and cannot be used against the claim.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d"
    },
    {
      "text": "The refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, run on the fare_breakdown and the trip_record: recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 11.0 + 0.28 x 22.0) x 1.1 surge) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP - 0 promo = 20.831; charged_total is 26.60; refund = 5.769, rounded up to SGD 5.80, with intermediate values unrounded as the policy requires. The multiplier of 1.1 is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier and from nowhere else. The refund exceeds the SGD 0.50 de minimis and is 21.7% of charged_total, so it is a PARTIAL_REFUND rather than a full refund; the contested SGD 5.80 is returned in full by that computation.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09115", "EV-TRIP-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare"
    },
    {
      "text": "The payment state shows the rider is presently carrying the disputed sum: fare_breakdown.payment_status is CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd is 0.0. Under POL-GEN-03 a NO_ACTION would leave that charge standing as the present state, so NO_ACTION is not a rider-favourable disposition on this file; only the POL-RD-02 partial refund, or an escalation that holds the money, leaves the rider not paying the contested SGD 5.80.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"]
    },
    {
      "text": "If the judge concludes that POL-RD-07(ii) bars establishment on the trace alone and that no independent corroboration exists, the correct outcome is still not NO_ACTION: POL-RD-07(iii) directs ESCALATE in precisely that situation, because an uncorroborated gap of this kind is a data failure and not a finding for the driver, and POL-RD-10(3) makes escalation mandatory where the trace is impaired under limbs (a) to (c) with no corroborating artifact of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names. An escalation holds the disputed SGD 5.80 rather than collecting it, so on that reading too the rider is not left carrying the charge.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-10"]
    }
  ]
}
